Z||000000||RiceBurner515||12-07-2000||06:26 PM||||has anyone ever shaved their door handles on their fiero? im thinking aobut it. you basically buy a kit and if you know how to do it you get rid of your door handles and have a keyless automatic door entry. how much are the kits? how much to have someone install?||||reg||1
Z||000001||fropuff||12-07-2000||08:30 PM||||If you wanted shaved handles, there would be no purpose to the side moldings, other than to cover up seams between panels.  There would be a big gap there where the handle was, or you could get rid of the moldings and bondo all the seams, but that would be stupid, in my opinion.  But, whatever you want to do...<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||12-08-2000||03:12 AM||||I knew someone who did that to his pick-up truck. The solenoids that popped the door open fried themselves out after about a year. He ended up putting in a power window kit to lower the window by remote to get in the car. He always thought the truck looked better without the door handles but hated opening the window to get in the truck. (Especially in rain or snow)||||reg||13
Z||000003||80's BOY||12-08-2000||10:55 AM||||yeah, when i stripped down my 85 gt i wanted to smooth out the lines by filling in the molding gap all the way around. no way to do it, because #1. the car flexes too much when driving. #2. the molding is incorporated into the rear clip, front fascia, door handles, etc. so i left that part of the project alone. i have shaved alot of s-10 door handles and it's pretty neat to do, just not a good idea on the Fiero.||||reg||13
